# StackHawk API Authentication Reference

The StackHawk platform REST API uses a two-step auth flow: exchange an API key for a
short-lived JWT, then present that JWT as a Bearer token on every subsequent request.

---

## Auth Flow Overview

1. **Exchange**: `POST`-equivalent `GET /api/v1/auth/login` with `X-ApiKey` header →
   returns a JWT in `.token`
2. **Use**: All API calls carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
3. **Expiry**: Tokens expire after **30 minutes**
4. **Re-auth**: On any `401` response, re-run the login call and retry the request
5. **Refresh (optional)**: `GET /api/v1/auth/refresh-token` with a valid Bearer token
   extends the session without re-submitting the API key

**Required environment variable:** `HAWK_API_KEY` — the same key used by the hawkscan
skill. Generate or retrieve one at **app.stackhawk.com → Settings → API Keys**.

---

## Quick Inline Auth

Get a token in a single line and store it in a shell variable:

```bash
HAWK_TOKEN=$(curl -s -H "X-ApiKey: ${HAWK_API_KEY}" \
  https://api.stackhawk.com/api/v1/auth/login | jq -r '.token')
```

Verify the token was returned (non-empty, not `null`):

```bash
[[ -z "${HAWK_TOKEN}" || "${HAWK_TOKEN}" == "null" ]] && \
  echo "ERROR: auth failed — check HAWK_API_KEY" && exit 1
```

---

## Using the Token

Pass the JWT as a Bearer token on every API request:

```bash
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer ${HAWK_TOKEN}" \
  https://api.stackhawk.com/api/v2/org/${ORG_ID}/apps
```

Replace `${ORG_ID}` with your organization UUID (visible in the StackHawk platform URL
or returned by `/api/v1/auth/login` in the `organization.id` field).

---

## Token Refresh

Extend an existing session without re-submitting the API key:

```bash
HAWK_TOKEN=$(curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer ${HAWK_TOKEN}" \
  https://api.stackhawk.com/api/v1/auth/refresh-token | jq -r '.token')
```

Use this when a long-running agent workflow approaches the 30-minute window. If the
token has already expired, this call will return `401` — fall back to the full login
flow using `HAWK_API_KEY`.

