## Pagination Reference

### V1 Endpoints

Identified by: path begins with `/api/v1/`

| Parameter | Location | Type | Description |
|-----------|----------|------|-------------|
| `pageSize` | query | integer | Max items per page |
| `pageToken` | query | integer | Offset token from previous response |

| Response field | Type | Description |
|----------------|------|-------------|
| `nextPageToken` | integer or absent | Present when more pages exist; absent or `null` on last page |

```bash
# Manual V1 pagination example
page_token=""
while true; do
  params="pageSize=100"
  [[ -n "${page_token}" ]] && params="${params}&pageToken=${page_token}"
  response=$(hawk_api GET "/api/v1/scan/${ORG_ID}?${params}")
  echo "${response}" | jq '.scans[]'
  page_token=$(echo "${response}" | jq -r '.nextPageToken // empty')
  [[ -z "${page_token}" ]] && break
done
```

### V2 Endpoints

Identified by: path begins with `/api/v2/`

| Parameter | Location | Type | Description |
|-----------|----------|------|-------------|
| `pageSize` | query | integer | Max items per page |
| `page` | query | string (`p_*`) | Cursor from `currentPage` of previous response |
| `pageToken` | query | string | Alias accepted by some V2 endpoints |

| Response field | Type | Description |
|----------------|------|-------------|
| `currentPage` | string | Cursor for this page; pass as `page` to get the next page |
| `hasNext` | boolean | `true` if more pages follow |
| `hasPrev` | boolean | `true` if previous pages exist |

```bash
# Manual V2 pagination example
page_cursor=""
while true; do
  params="pageSize=100"
  [[ -n "${page_cursor}" ]] && params="${params}&page=${page_cursor}"
  response=$(hawk_api GET "/api/v2/org/${ORG_ID}/apps?${params}")
  echo "${response}" | jq '.applications[]'
  has_next=$(echo "${response}" | jq -r '.hasNext // false')
  [[ "${has_next}" != "true" ]] && break
  page_cursor=$(echo "${response}" | jq -r '.currentPage')
done
```

**Use `hawk_api_all_pages` instead of manual loops** — it handles both V1 and V2
automatically based on the response shape.

